  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adola-Hasasa Resilient Livelihood Promotion Program Phase II (2026-2028)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on a legacy of phase I significantly reduced the household food gap for 78% of families and dramatically boosted women&apos;s participation in decision-making. Phase II focused on strengthening last phase initiatives. The goal is to ensure food security, women&#x2019;s socio-economy, and enhance peaceful coexistence. The project contributed to women&apos;s empowerment, stabilize family income through crop diversification, and enhance community ties through strengthened local peace-building. Guided by Rights-Based Approach (RBA) principles, the initiative champions accountability and non-discrimination. Its reach is ambitious aiming to directly benefit 21,730 people including 10,000 new targets focusing on the most vulnerable like female-headed households and landless youth. From design to execution, active stakeholder and community involvement will ensure this critical work endures.</narrative>
  </description>
